  "interactionBehavior": {
    "summary": "Surface is not a control. It paints a fill and stamps `data-surface`, `data-surface-step`, and `data-appearance` so children remap their tokens — that is the entire behaviour. It is a `<div>` by default, not in the tab order, with no cursor, hover, press, or focus halo. HTML attributes in `...rest` are forwarded, so a caller *can* add `onClick` / `tabIndex`, but Surface itself never does. Default `mode` is `ghost` (same step as the parent; fill is `--Surface-Self-Color` or transparent). Use Card's `interactive` (or a real Button) when the region itself must be clickable."
  },
